cbf0fb621888596aa14ad5f2349b503e23b1b72d:tests/evidence/cloud-takeover-20261009/source-authority-43-public-v4/source-authority-243/authority/issue123-43-current640-source-audit.md:9:3. **B7**: `index.html:384` includes `[data-shape-action="hole"]` under the shape operations, while `:388` already has `[data-face-tool="hole"]` and R. `app.js:10305` confirms the shape entry does only `feSetTool("hole")`, exactly the same action as the standalone/R entry. S3 explicitly adopts tool deduplication while preserving R/current contracts. The minimal merge is to remove this duplicate shape-menu choice while retaining the standalone hole button, `feSetTool("hole")`, shortcut R and all native hole semantics. Other shape operations remain. This is the only confirmed identical-command duplicate; guide/timber/grid placement versus forms are distinct actions.
